WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
<b>Banquet of Fire</b>

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.540
Are you Auctioneer?

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.600
Indeed I am.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.800
Wait, Alma. Where's Alma?!

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.850
She's fine. We picked her up for you.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.030
Who's "we"?

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.450
Number 11?

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.330
Are you Beta?

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:26.460
No. Sorry to say that 
I am not the "Beta" you seek.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.440
Then why do you have that?

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:33.460
I can't tell you any more 
as long as you remain a police pawn.

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:36.400
The cops have control of your little body.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:41.590
They have the power to turn you back 
into just a brain-in-a-box.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:43.490
So what?

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:47.830
I can rescue you from them.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.630
But in return, you must give me your word

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:57.870
that you will cut all ties with them 
and side with me instead.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.870
Oh, and that you'll stay away 
from Jinkoku-sha, too.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.180
What?

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:08.700
The Counter EX-ARM squad is a thorn in my side. 
You in particular, Natsume Akira.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:14.720
<b>Tokyo Bay Megafloat - A Stage</b>

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.550
They won't find us here.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.580
How's the president doing?

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.350
He's sleeping after taking his medication.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.660
How's the search?

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.730
Can't find anything.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.690
Alma's coordinates aren't showing up at all.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:36.110
<i>And Akira's connection is still
blocked off after the hack.</i>

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.190
We'll have to unplug his mains.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.250
Why do you care about Jinkoku-sha?

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.870
I've teamed up with Al Jarde 
in order to further my goals.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:50.890
His terms were to isolate Jinkoku-sha.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:53.230
Wait. <i>He</i> was the one out to get them?

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:57.150
Forget about Jinkoku-sha and work with me.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.720
You want to go back 
to being human, don't you?

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:04.760
Man, you already know 
there's no way I'd accept, right?

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:09.500
And, well, congrats! My answer is no!

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:14.070
I did indeed expect this 
from you, Natsume Akira.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:21.760
But you <i>will</i> join me eventually.
And that's not a prediction. It's a spoiler.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:27.000
That is your destiny 
as EX-ARM Number 00 Alpha.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.430
What's that supposed to mean?

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:31.660
Neither the police 
nor Jinkoku-sha deserve your help.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.300
Look into the Water Purification Plant terror
attack in Berdeen, and you'll know why.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.120
Huh? I'm back?

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.310
Akira! You're okay!

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:21.530
<b>Counter EX-ARM Squad HQ</b>

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:21.000
What's that damn Auctioneer playing at?

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.360
Wait. You met Auctioneer?

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.320
Yeah. He's in cahoots with Al Jarde.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.120
Al Jarde was the one out to get Jinkoku-sha!

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.120
Alisa, tell me something.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.830
<i>What's this Berdeen plant terror attack?</i>

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.990
Must be the 2023 bombing 
of the water purification plant

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:44.120
that local and Japanese firms were building.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.480
Do you think there could be a link 
between that and this auction?

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.340
The case file can't be accessed. 
It's classified.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.850
I'm fairly certain that 
Grandfather was part of the project.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:55.910
What?

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:00.000
Wait, Al Jarde is a citizen 
of the Berdeen Republic.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.490
So if he's trying to take out Jinkoku-sha, 
that must mean...

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:06.490
Shit's getting complicated again.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.790
We haven't figured out 
where Jinkoku-sha ran off to yet.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:22.440
They can run and hide all they want, 
but we will find them.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.650
And exact our revenge.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.070
What is it?

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.760
I'm detecting some unusual activity nearby.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.280
I'll go check it out.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.090
Do that.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:49.070
Happy birthday, Sis.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.520
It's a set.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.350
Thanks, Soma!

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:58.550
I'll keep this with me forever!

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:09.290
Keeping watch? Thank you.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.310
Uh, may I ask you something?

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:16.710
Why didn't you answer the question 
about the plant earlier?

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:22.140
Didn't you lose your family in that incident?

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:23.570
How do you know that?

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:26.740
Because it's my job to know.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:30.890
I haven't really come to terms with it yet.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:34.250
I suppose we still don't know 
who was behind it.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:40.290
But wait. Given what Al Jarde's doing now, 
maybe he was the one behind it?

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.280
Wait, what?

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.810
Oh, uh, I was just thinking aloud!

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:47.860
Public Safety doesn't have 
any intel on it, either!

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.070
Where are you going, Minami?

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.480
Please don't tell me 
you're going to see Al Jarde.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.930
Did you forget we're here on a mission?

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:01.920
Sorry, I have to go.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:02.900
Minami!

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:11.820
Minami ran off by herself? 
Why didn't you stop her?

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:16.000
<i>I-I'm sorry! If you saw the look 
in her eyes, you'd know why!</i>

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.620
<i>She's probably going to see Al Jarde!</i>

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.210
You good to go, Akira?

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.050
Yeah!

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:26.590
Man, what the hell is Minami thinking?

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:30.630
<b>Tokyo Bay Megafloat</b>

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:35.760
I'll let the Spiritus duo handle Jinkoku-sha,

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.310
and Bathala will take care of Al Jarde.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:42.490
Y'know, the way you talk gets on my nerves.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:46.510
I'm not gonna destroy Jinkoku-sha on your orders. 
I'm doing it because I want to.

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:47.690
Let's go, Aristarif.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.490
You're up, Ivo.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.990
Yikes, yikes, yikes!

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.370
He's in the penthouse.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:08.600
Akira?

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:12.360
You trying a solo raid? 
Who do you think you are?

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:16.090
I know it's stupid. 
But I need to talk to Al Jarde.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.770
Wait, what?

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:25.940
It's you!

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:30.310
I'm here to ask you something.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:34.880
Tell me about the Berdeen
plant terror attack.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.120
Minami?

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.660
Are you sure you want to know,

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:40.360
Uezono Minami?

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:43.520
How do you know her name?

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:46.150
You were a victim of that attack.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:50.680
Minami... a victim?!

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.630
Why did I have to lose my family?

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:55.080
You know the reason. I know you do!

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:05.440
Eight years ago, the long reign of religious
fanatics over Berdeen finally ended.

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:09.230
As head of the reinstated emirate family,

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:11.570
I hoped to rebuild the nation 
from the ground up.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:18.910
At the time, I was working on the joint
plant project with the Japanese firms.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:23.010
I had a wife, Lamia, and a son, Arim.

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:25.800
They both had luckily survived the civil war,

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.540
and we were soon blessed 
with a daughter, Malaika.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.700
Our country was abound with poverty.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:35.400
I saw it as my duty 
to lead it to better days,

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.800
to ensure a brighter future 
for the generations to come.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:42.890
But all it took was one missile 
from an unidentified drone—

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:46.040
one moment—to take everything 
away from me.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.070
And I swore to myself

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:58.870
that I would do whatever it takes 
to find who was responsible

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.410
and make them pay with their own blood.

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:04.550
So, did you find them?

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:07.140
It was Hayama Gaho.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:12.180
The man you're guarding. 
The leader of Jinkoku-sha.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.400
No!

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.000
He killed my uncle, who was against
the inflow of foreign capital,

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.640
and took over the entire plant project.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:22.680
So...

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:32.280
You attacked the plant as payback?

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:42.420
He killed your family?

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.210
The one behind that attack was...

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:53.420
<i>His voice just cut out. 
No, all sound just dropped out!</i>

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:10.640
Ivo, move on to stage two.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:15.610
Enjoy his magic field, 
where nobody can see or hear anything!

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.900
<i>This is trouble.</i>

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:24.780
<i>I've got my night-vision mode, 
but these two...</i>

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.270
<i>Wait, is she planning to fight in the dark?</i>

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:29.750
Minami! Behind you!

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.670
<i>Where'd he go?</i>

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:02.450
Sound is back. Turn on the lights.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.080
Truly a shame.

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:11.790
Bathala will be dropping out 
of this race, I take it?

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:13.100
Damn it!

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:15.750
Why? Whywhywhy... Why?!

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.790
Because I am a man of the desert.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:20.880
The sands hold no scents.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:24.550
That makes us sensitive 
to the scents in the air.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:29.930
The faint smell of blood splatters on you 
told me exactly where you were.

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:33.180
But how'd you evade his attacks?

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:34.940
Simple.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.440
All I had to do was 
feel the touch of his knife on my body

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:40.230
and avoid it before it pierced me through.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.220
Ah, yes, like taking candy from a baby.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:43.350
<i>We've got trouble!</i>

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:46.860
Somebody's leaked the location 
of Jinkoku-sha's hideout!

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:48.580
We don't know who it is!

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:52.910
It's probably been sent 
to all the groups in the auction!

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:58.670
Looks like we strike first.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:04.820
Do your thing, Aristarif. Fight well for me.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.970
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:16.320
W-Well, didn't take them long to get here.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:17.900
Spiritus, eh?

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.190
Bah, fine. I'll hold them off.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.350
Hold them off? You want to go out there?!

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:26.400
We can't just sit around when they're
right there. It's do-or-die, bucko.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:27.930
That's not ideal!

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:29.390
Get your bossman on the line.

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:30.990
Huh? O-Okay.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.370
I think it's about time 
you filled us in, bro.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:39.670
Who's the brains behind this operation? 
What exactly are we guarding here?

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:43.040
Well...

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.380
Go ahead.

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:47.590
It's the Restoration Bloc.

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:53.930
Officially called the Japanese Restoration Bloc,

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:58.360
it was a group formed after the Tokyo Attack 
to rebuild the city and Japan.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:00.920
Allowed to take extralegal measures,

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.300
it's filled with people 
key to Japan's revival.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:08.280
Grandfather is one of its members, as well.

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:11.080
Hah. I get it now.

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:15.540
We're fine with things as they stand. 
Put us through to Ichigaya.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:16.330
Sir!

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:20.380
Please wait!

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:24.670
My grandfather and I don't deserve 
to be protected with your life.

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:27.260
We can stop them by turning ourselves in.

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:28.880
I'm afraid that's not an option!

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:34.070
If you feel you don't deserve our protection, 
just become someone who does.

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:37.060
Miyabe, handle things here.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:41.230
Got it! I'll keep her safe, no matter what!

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:43.990
<i>Please be safe.</i>

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:52.200
<b>Tokyo Bay Megafloat - D Stage</b>

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:51.450
I wasn't behind the plant attack.

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:54.720
It was the remnants of the fanatical terrorists.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:58.780
By the time I got there, 
it was all too late.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:00.540
Except for you two.

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:02.910
"You two"?

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:05.550
So he really is...

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:07.670
That's right, Sis.

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:12.050
I'm Soma, your little brother.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:14.360
Minami's bro?!

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:18.600
It really is you. Soma...

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:24.900
I'm so glad you're alive!

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.030
I'm happy for you, Minami.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:32.020
Soma? What happened to your body?

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:37.190
Soma was on the brink of death 
when I got there.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.370
Everything but his head 
had to be fitted with cybernetics.

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.590
That, of course, is a surgery banned by law.

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:46.440
If he underwent it, 
he could never go home to Japan,

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:49.340
but I put his life first.

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:51.320
No...

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:53.560
Sis, please.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:59.040
Quit guarding Jinkoku-sha 
and leave this island.

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:01.480
What are you saying? Why would you...

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:07.190
The two of us swore to ourselves to make
Hayama Gaho suffer more than we did.

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:12.870
We will kill all of his family
and friends, every last one of them.

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:16.200
We'll kill his granddaughter before his eyes, 
and then kill him!

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:18.810
He'll know what it means 
to pay with his blood!

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:25.920
N-No, you can't! Please listen to me, Soma!

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:30.620
You finally got to see your long-lost
brother, so why is this happening?

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:34.890
We're ready to move out.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:35.680
Let's go.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.200
Go where? To kill Hayama Gaho?!

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:39.960
Do you really need me to spell it out?

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:43.730
Our mom and dad never asked for this!

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:48.740
You didn't watch them die before your eyes.

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:51.160
That's why you can spout this bullshit.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:56.860
I'll get my revenge on everyone who
put me through this, by any means necessary.

00:16:58.440 --> 00:16:59.500
Soma...

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:08.750
Aristarif's EX-ARM lets him control 
the oscillation of iron atoms.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.420
Surely you don't think 
you can beat him all by yourself.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:20.220
Gah! Kondo!

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:25.140
<i>After the Tokyo Attack,</i>

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:30.150
<i>Jinkoku-sha pulled the strings behind
military projects, domestic and international</i>

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.710
<i>to attain the influence we wield today.</i>

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:36.530
<i>While we did it to rebuild our nation,</i>

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:40.490
<i>the fact remains that we caused untold
amounts of tragedy across the world.</i>

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:46.300
<i>Having been raised by that blood money,</i>

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:50.300
<i>I am practically clad head-to-toe 
in my grandfather's sins.</i>

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:55.060
<i>It's only natural that I'm just as much 
a target of hate as Jinkoku-sha is.</i>

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:02.350
If you feel you don't deserve our protection, 
just become someone who does.

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:31.180
Your ability works only on iron!

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.660
But I'm all flesh and bone! 
It can't do shit to me!

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:39.940
Aristarif!

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:48.680
These bees get a B-minus in discipline!

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:54.010
Wait... Yggdrasil?!

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:55.780
Please, call me "Ygg."

00:18:56.420 --> 00:19:01.030
We met your avatar in the VR world, 
and now you're out here?!

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:03.050
Please be okay, Akira.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:06.310
Soma!

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:10.540
A quest for revenge? I won't let you!

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.140
Can you really shoot your own brother?

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:17.150
I don't want to.

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:19.400
So please, just stop!

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:22.590
Alma.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:30.520
Put your gun down, Minami.

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:31.800
Alma?

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:36.820
At this range, I can neutralize you 
faster than you can fire.

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:40.280
Wait. What are you saying, Alma?

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.590
I won't let you shoot my master.

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:45.330
Did they mess with her AI?!

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:50.040
As I said, by any means necessary.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:53.450
What? Not Alma...

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:56.000
I know! My quantum network!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:20:00.520
No point, Akira. We've already cut it off.

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:03.930
We're going to do it, Sis.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.810
We'll be on opposing sides next time we meet.

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:08.970
Alma and I won't show any mercy.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:11.920
No!

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:14.060
Soma!

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.330
You really fired, Sis.

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:27.420
This makes us enemies for real.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:35.240
I... I fired my gun at Soma.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:40.460
I finally got to see him again. 
How did things end up like this?

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:45.800
Soma!

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:52.520
What?!

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:57.600
<i>What's all this dwama about?</i>

00:20:57.600 --> 00:20:59.770
<i>Did you all forget why you're here?</i>

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:04.600
<i>A reunion between long-wost sibwings?</i>

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:07.620
<i>A revenge pwot decades in the making?</i>

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:12.040
<i>A hero protecting his pwincess?</i>

00:21:12.550 --> 00:21:14.710
<i>You certainly don't look 
very heroic right now.</i>

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:17.080
What in the blue hell?

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:20.940
<i>I went through all that twouble 
to tell y'all where Jinkoku-sha was,</i>

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:25.340
<i>but you wouldn't do anything,
so I went and ahead and captured them myself.</i>

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:27.690
<i>See?</i>

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:31.180
You...

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:32.770
Who the hell are you?

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:35.000
<i>Who, me?</i>

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:37.770
<i>I'm Beta.</i>

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:39.460
Beta...?

00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:42.610
<i>I told you we'd meet again.</i>

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:46.070
Beta...

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:50.090
You're going down!

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:27.590
Hewwo! Who am I, you ask?

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:30.080
Y'all swacked off too hard!

00:23:30.080 --> 00:23:33.150
So I'm taking over and making things hype!

00:23:33.150 --> 00:23:36.300
Next time, on <i>EX-ARM:</i> 
"Battle 008 - Beta."

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Beta</b>

00:23:36.300 --> 00:23:39.450
Let's begin! It's time to partay!
